<p>Fixed to the front of the clock case in the north transept of Chester Cathedral is a poem by Henry Twells (1823–1900):</p>
<p>When as a child I laughed and wept,<br />
Time crept.<br />
When as a youth I waxed more bold,<br />
Time <em>strolled</em>.<br />
When I became a full grown man,<br />
Time RAN.<br />
When older still I daily grew,<br />
Time <em>FLEW</em>.<br />
Soon I shall find, in passing on,<br />
Time <em>gone</em>.<br />
O Christ! wilt Thou have saved me then?<br />
Amen.</p>
<p>He called it &#8220;Time&#8217;s Paces.&#8221;</p>
